[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-agent.cxd — the agent surface's page,
   repo-cx-platform-agent.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 4).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the
   tools suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-agent
  [intro
    """**TL;DR — an agent is a peer, and its messages are ordinary values.**
       `cx-platform-agent` is the tool and agent-protocol surface: a tool
       descriptor is projected from a command definition at list time, an
       MCP request or an A2A message is a CX value shaped to its wire form,
       and any callable — a def, a closure, a tool behind a transport —
       composes through one Runnable convention."""]
  [body
    """The projection is the point: a `[?def]` that carries an `[effects]`
       clause is a command, and its descriptor — name, description, input
       and output schema, the read-only and destructive annotations — derives
       from the definition and its documentation when the tools are listed,
       never from a hand-kept manifest, so a tool cannot say one thing and do
       another. A feature grammar projects the same way: an observe verb is a
       read-only tool, an act verb its complement, and two features that
       share a verb name export two distinct tools."""]
  [body
    """The protocols compose the substrate this site already documents —
       JSON-RPC, JSON Schema, the HTTP client — with no new transport: the
       MCP client builds and reads the initialize, list-tools and call-tool
       exchanges, the server half answers them from the same projection, and
       the A2A client shapes messages and tasks and records a task's
       lifecycle in a hash-chained journal, so its history replays and
       verifies. `run` is the algebra over all of it — invoke, batch, pipe,
       compose, fan out — `llm` is the first Runnable, and `adjudicate` turns
       a review band's pairs into resolution records an agent decided and a
       later run consumes deterministically."""]
  [gives
    """Eight modules of the platform group, pure CX with no V build: the tool
       projection, the MCP client and server, A2A and its journal binding,
       the Runnable algebra, the LLM provider and the adjudicator. Each links
       to the reference page projected from its own documentation, and their
       sources keep the `x/` path they graduated from."""]
  [try
    """A command definition with an empty `[effects]` clause and its
       documentation, projected to a tool descriptor: the summary is the
       description, the parameter is the input schema, and the empty effect
       set is inside the read-only set, so the annotations say read-only and
       not destructive — a command still, because the clause is present."""]
  [fixture id=tools-004-zero-item-effects-is-a-command]
  [status
    """The agent surface ships as a package: its eight modules are bundled
       into the build from the pin, its specification and corpus travel with
       it, and its own repository grades the pins, the lint, the corpus and
       the lanes before the front door moves the pin."""]]
